---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Promised Trillion Dollar AI-Coding Market"
  description="About: The Promised Trillion Dollar AI-Coding Market. Economics essay in the OpenIE research catalog."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Economics essay · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      The Promised Trillion Dollar AI-Coding Market
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The economics companion to the Reality Code Engine (RCE) research paper, and the place where its theory and economics meet. It sets out who projects the AI coding market and what they project: about $3 trillion a year in developer value, company-reported revenue and valuations, token volume, a filed loss, capex and data-centre energy. Each number carries its source and a label: projection, company-reported, survey estimate, filed or measured.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      Every projection assumes one path to autonomous computer automation: high energy, high compute, per-token rent and the model in the loop forever. RCE measures a second path. With correctness as the gate and joules as the ranking, on held-out test splits with 0 model calls it repaired 520,541 of 520,821 one-token faults and 63.7% of 21,320 real single-statement Java bugs with the whole file, at hundredths of a reported joule per solved task. Where that path covers a task, its price falls toward the energy to run it, as Spell Check fell to a bundled zero price.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
      Projections and measurements are kept in separate labels. The trillion is a cited value estimate, not a revenue forecast. Open questions are stated as propositions with protocols. The engineering and the measurements are in the research paper.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2" id="companion">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Companion paper</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">The engineering, theory and measured results are in <a href="/papers/rce/" class="text-brand-cyan">The Reality Code Engine: One Form, Many Fits, and the Low-Entropy Path to Autonomous Coding</a> (<a href="/about/rce/" class="text-brand-cyan">about</a>).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/ai-coding-market/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read paper → /papers/ai-coding-market/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/ai-coding-market.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/figures/rce/intent-entropy.svg" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/30 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Figure: intent and entropy
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
